<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<article xmlns="http://jats.nlm.nih.gov/publishing/1.2" article-type="guideline" dtd-version="1.2">
  <front>
    <article-meta>
      <title-group>
        <article-title>Sample Functional Dyspepsia Guideline</article-title>
      </title-group>
    </article-meta>
    <abstract>
      <sec>
        <title>Summary</title>
        <p>First-line therapy is a proton pump inhibitor for uninvestigated dyspepsia.</p>
      </sec>
    </abstract>
  </front>
  <body>
    <sec id="intro" sec-type="intro">
      <title>Introduction</title>
      <p>Functional dyspepsia affects up to 20 percent of adults.</p>
      <p>Symptoms include epigastric pain and postprandial fullness.</p>
    </sec>
    <sec id="treatment" sec-type="treatment">
      <title>Treatment</title>
      <p>Start PPI therapy for functional dyspepsia when alarm features are absent.</p>
      <sec id="first-line">
        <title>First-line</title>
        <p>Omeprazole 20 mg once daily for four to eight weeks.</p>
      </sec>
      <sec id="second-line">
        <title>Second-line</title>
        <p>Consider tricyclic antidepressants when PPIs fail.</p>
      </sec>
    </sec>
    <sec id="refs" sec-type="refs">
      <title>References</title>
      <ref-list>
        <ref id="ref1"><label>1</label><element-citation>Example citation only.</element-citation></ref>
      </ref-list>
    </sec>
  </body>
</article>
